# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ROSW — repo-root attribute rules
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Line endings ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# plugins/ui-design/maintenance/evaluate-relevance.py fingerprints the raw bytes
# of the catalog's runtime and data files, and of its own oracle inputs, and
# refuses to run when they drift. On a machine with core.autocrlf=true a plain
# checkout rewrites every one of those files to CRLF and changes the hash, so the
# whole plugin is pinned to LF on every platform. After a deliberate change to a
# fingerprinted file, regenerate the fingerprints with that script.
#
# The plugin also carries its own plugins/ui-design/.gitattributes, because it is
# published on its own and this root rule does not travel with it. Both say the
# same thing; validate-contract.py checks the plugin's.
plugins/ui-design/** text eol=lf
